From abf6b6ae7a905f994febe00edde0948a3455af8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Yang <eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Feb 2026 09:32:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] transport: af-mctp: Fix TID lookup with MCTP_NET_ANY

The pldm_transport_af_mctp_map_tid() API stores mappings with
tid_map[tid].net = MCTP_NET_ANY (0), but get_tid() requires exact match
(tid_map[i].net == network). When MCTP messages arrive with non-zero
network ID, the lookup fails, causing pldmd to crash with "free():
invalid pointer" errors.

Allow MCTP_NET_ANY in stored mappings to act as a wildcard matching any
incoming network ID, while still supporting exact matches for explicitly
stored network values.

Change-Id: Iaf9a0e09681dbfd202af747688b160dba1558692
Signed-off-by: Eric Yang <eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com>
---
 src/transport/af-mctp.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/transport/af-mctp.c b/src/transport/af-mctp.c
index 84d5211..9d3b487 100644
--- a/src/transport/af-mctp.c
+++ b/src/transport/af-mctp.c
@@ -88,7 +88,9 @@ static int pldm_transport_af_mctp_get_tid(struct pldm_transport_af_mctp *ctx,
 {
 	if (network != 0 && eid != 0) {
 		for (int i = 0; i < PLDM_MAX_TIDS; i++) {
-			if (ctx->tid_map[i].net == network &&
+			/* Allow MCTP_NET_ANY (0) to match any network for backward compatibility */
+			if ((ctx->tid_map[i].net == MCTP_NET_ANY ||
+			     ctx->tid_map[i].net == network) &&
 			    ctx->tid_map[i].eid == eid) {
 				*tid = i;
 				return 0;
-- 
